    <string name="hh_rec_note">Station (SIP) calls are recorded on both sides. SIM calls: Android only lets the app record the microphone, so the other person is clearly audible mainly on speaker. Recording a conversation may require the other person’s consent.</string>
    <string name="hh_rec_sim_a11y">For SIM calls, turn on the “HHPhone call recording” accessibility service: without it Android mutes the microphone during a call. If the switch is greyed out: App info → ⋮ → Allow restricted settings.</string>
    <string name="hh_rec_a11y_auto">For SIM calls the accessibility service is turned on automatically only during the call — banking apps don’t see it the rest of the time.</string>
    <string name="hh_rec_a11y_adb">Banking apps won’t open while the accessibility service is on. HHPhone can turn it on only during SIM calls — this needs a one-time permission. With a computer: adb shell pm grant %1$s android.permission.WRITE_SECURE_SETTINGS</string>
    <string name="hh_adb_need_dev">Without a computer: first enable Developer options — About phone → Software information → tap “Build number” 7 times.</string>
    <string name="hh_adb_open_about">Open “About phone”</string>
    <string name="hh_adb_steps">Without a computer (Wi-Fi needed): tap the button, turn on “Wireless debugging”, open it, tap “Pair device with pairing code”, then pull down the notification shade and type the 6 digits into the HHPhone notification. Keep the code window open.</string>
